0235   E1                     POP   HL   
0236   C9                     RET      
0237                             ; /~ ( row col addr -- ): the two cells under the string's address go. In
0237                             ; the checked build "$" is the routine prstr: its own return address goes
0237                             ; first, and hp1 calls it again afterwards. There a /~ that takes cells
0237                             ; that aren"t there is s after the "$' (or at its NUL: see e_dollar), as for
0237                             ; any other character. chkstk stops a /~ only when the stack is already
0237                             ; past its empty place, so that, however many there are, what they write
0237                             ; stays in the spare bytes above the stack.
0237                PAT:         
0237                          IF   CHECKED   
                              POP   DE   
                              CALL   chkstk   
0237                          ENDIF      
